# Broadcom publishes the driver over https with no detached signature and no
# signing key, so there is nothing for uscan to verify against. pgpmode=none
# says that honestly rather than pretending to a check that cannot happen.
#
# What actually protects this package is not the transport: every artefact is
# pinned by SHA256 in SHA256SUMS, and a file whose bytes do not match the pin is
# refused outright rather than treated as a reason to try somewhere else.
libfprint-2-tod1-broadcom-installer source: debian-watch-does-not-check-openpgp-signature [debian/watch]
